./contributingGuides/FORMS.md:102:Additionally, pressing the enter key on any focused field should submit the form.
./contributingGuides/FORMS.md:116:3. On submit, repeat validation and submit with the clean value.
./contributingGuides/FORMS.md:136:All form fields will additionally be validated when the form is submitted. Although we are validating on blur this additional step is necessary to cover edge cases where forms are auto-filled or when a form is submitted by pressing enter (i.e. there will be only a ‘submit’ event and no ‘blur’ event to hook into).
./contributingGuides/FORMS.md:191:When any form field fails to validate in addition to the inline error below a field, an error message will also appear inline above the submit button indicating that some fields need to be fixed. A “fix the errors” link will scroll the user to the first input that needs attention and focus on it (putting the cursor at the end of the existing value). By default, on form submit and when tapping the “fix the errors” link we should scroll the user to the first field that needs their attention.
./contributingGuides/FORMS.md:197:Server errors related to form submission should appear in the Form Alert above the submit button. They should not appear in growls or other kinds of alerts. Additionally, as best practice moving forward server errors should never solely do the work that frontend validation can also do. This means that any error that can be validated in the frontend should be validated in the frontend and backend.
./contributingGuides/FORMS.md:206:Submit buttons shall not be disabled or blocked from being pressed in most cases. We will allow the user to submit a form and point them in the right direction if anything needs their attention.
./contributingGuides/FORMS.md:208:The only time we won’t allow a user to press the submit button is when we have submitted the form and are waiting for a response (e.g. from the API). In this case, we will show a loading indicator and additional taps on the submit button will have no effect. This is handled by the Form component and will also ensure that a form cannot be submitted multiple times.
./contributingGuides/OFFLINE_UX.md:102:This pattern greys out the submit button on a form and does not allow the form to be submitted. We also show a "You appear offline" message near the bottom of the screen. Importantly, we _do_ let the user fill out the form fields. That data gets saved locally so they don’t have to fill it out again once online.
./contributingGuides/OFFLINE_UX.md:148:  - An easy way to tell if something is a form is to try and find a submit button. If a submit button is present or if the user is filling out form inputs, answer YES to this question.
